    "StringPadInteger[num] converts the integer num to a string and pads it \
with zeros to length 3.\nStringPadInteger[{num, len}] converts the integer \
num to a string and pads it with zeros to length len.\nStringPadInteger[pre, \
num] the same but with prefix pre.\nStringPadInteger[pre, {num, len}] the \
same but with prefix pre.\nStringPadInteger[num, post] the same but with \
postfix post.\nStringPadInteger[{num, len}, post] the same but with postfix \
post.\nStringPadInteger[pre, num, post] the same but with pre and postfix pre \
and post.\nStringPadInteger[post, {num, len}, post] the same but with pre and \
postfix pre and post.", 
